1
00:04:35,294 --> 00:04:41,294
His story became a legend. His adventure is one you'll never forget.

2
00:09:10,588 --> 00:09:16,588
Balto is a family, animation, adventure film directed by Simon Wells.

3
00:13:45,882 --> 00:13:51,882
An outcast half-wolf risks his life to prevent a deadly
epidemic from ravaging Nome, Alaska.

4
00:18:21,176 --> 00:18:27,176
Balto (voice), played by Kevin Bacon.

5
00:22:56,470 --> 00:23:02,470
Boris the Goose (voice), played by Bob Hoskins.

6
00:27:31,764 --> 00:27:37,764
Jenna (voice), played by Bridget Fonda.

7
00:32:07,058 --> 00:32:13,058
Steele the Sled Dog (voice), played by Jim Cummings.

8
00:36:42,352 --> 00:36:48,352
Muk and Luk (voice), played by Phil Collins.

9
00:41:17,647 --> 00:41:23,647
Young Rosy (voice), played by Juliette Brewer.

10
00:45:52,941 --> 00:45:58,941
Balto is a 1995 animated adventure film directed by Simon Wells, produced by
Amblin Entertainment, and distributed by Universal Pictures.

11
00:50:28,235 --> 00:50:34,235
It is loosely based on the true story of the dog Balto who helped save
children infected with diphtheria in the 1925 serum run to Nome.

12
00:55:03,529 --> 00:55:09,529
The film stars voice actors Kevin Bacon, Bridget
Fonda, Phil Collins, and Bob Hoskins.

13
00:59:38,823 --> 00:59:44,823
Though primarily an animated film, it uses a live-action framing device that takes place in New York
City's Central Park and features Miriam Margolyes as an older version of one of the children.

14
01:04:14,117 --> 01:04:20,117
This is the third and final film to be produced by Steven Spielberg's
Amblimation animation studio, before the studio's closure in 1997.

15
01:08:49,411 --> 01:08:55,411
Released theatrically in the United States on December 22, 1995, the film was a financial failure due to being overshadowed by the release of Toy Story, but
its subsequent sales on home video led to two direct-to-video sequels: Balto II: Wolf Quest (2002) and Balto III: Wings of Change (2004).

16
01:13:24,705 --> 01:13:30,705
The film explores themes of wolf, pet, cartoon, villain, dog-sledding race.
